  "answer": "### **Loan Amortization Calculation Sheet**\n\n**Project:** Equipment Loan Payment Analysis\n**Date:** October 26, 2023\n\n---\n\n#### **1. Input Parameters**\n| Parameter | Symbol | Value |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Principal Loan Amount | $P$ | $\\$250,000.00$ |\n| Annual Percentage Rate (APR) | $APR$ | $7\\%$ ($0.07$) |\n| Loan Term | $t$ | $5$ Years |\n| Payment Frequency | $f$ | Monthly ($12$ payments/year) |\n| Monthly Interest Rate | $r$ | $0.07 \\div 12 \\approx 0.0058333333$ |\n| Total Number of Payments | $n$ | $5 \\times 12 = 60$ |\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Formula**\nTo calculate the fixed monthly payment, we use the standard amortization formula derived from the present value of an ordinary annuity:\n\n$$M = P \\frac{r(1+r)^n}{(1+r)^n - 1}$$\n\nWhere:\n*   **$M$** = Total monthly payment\n*   **$P$** = Principal loan amount\n*   **$r$** = Monthly interest rate\n*   **$n$** = Total number of months\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Step-by-Step Calculation**\nTo ensure absolute precision and avoid rounding errors, calculations are performed using high-precision decimals.\n\n**Step A: Calculate the growth factor $(1+r)^n$**\n$$(1 + \\frac{0.07}{12})^{60} \\approx (1.0058333333)^{60} \\approx 1.41762526$$\n\n**Step B: Calculate the numerator $r(1+r)^n$**\n$$0.0058333333 \\times 1.41762526 \\approx 0.00826948$$\n\n**Step C: Calculate the denominator $(1+r)^n - 1$**\n$$1.41762526 - 1 = 0.41762526$$\n\n**Step D: Solve for $M$**\n$$M = 250,000 \\times \\left( \\frac{0.00826948}{0.41762526} \\right)$$\n$$M = 250,000 \\times 0.0198011985$$\n$$M = 4,950.2996...$$\n\n---\n\n#### **4. Final Result**\n**Monthly Payment:** **$\\$4,950.30$**",
